entric, not willing to further education. For C: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, not open to new ideas, not good at taking criticism, unorganized.\n\nMake argument: A's reliability ensures consistent performance, crew atmosphere indicates cooperation, quick decisions and calmness meet stress resilience. C's technical strengths are important but his lack of openness to new ideas and criticism could impair crew cooperation and adaptability, which are equally safety-critical. Since we have no evidence that C can accept feedback, the risk is higher. Therefore I maintain recommendation for A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate A."}
